# Line-ending policy.
#
# This is a mixed-OS repo whose selfhost gates depend on byte identity, and
# developer machines run with core.autocrlf=true. Without this file, any tool
# that writes LF (or strips CR) produces phantom-modified files and
# OS-dependent bytes. Policy: every text file is LF in the repo AND in the
# working tree; git never converts behind our backs.
#
# The index is already uniformly LF (verified via `git ls-files --eol` before
# this file was added), so this introduces no renormalization churn.

* text=auto eol=lf

# Windows cmd batch files are the one place CRLF in the working tree is the
# safer convention (cmd.exe label/goto parsing edge cases). Repo copy stays LF.
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf

# Known binaries: never subject to text heuristics or conversion.
bin/cryo binary
bin/cryo.exe binary
*.exe binary
*.dll binary
*.a binary
*.o binary
*.obj binary
*.png binary
*.ico binary
*.icns binary
*.ai binary
*.eps binary
*.pdf binary
*.zip binary
